<body class="bg-gray-50 text-gray-800 font-sans">

    <nav class="bg-white border-b border-gray-200 sticky top-0 z-50">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-4 flex justify-between items-center">
            <a href="index.html#projects" class="text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 text-sm font-medium inline-flex items-center">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left mr-2"></i> Back to Portfolio
            </a>
            <span class="text-xs bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 font-semibold px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md border border-blue-100">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-file-code mr-1"></i> System Architecture Model
            </span>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <header class="bg-white py-12 border-b border-gray-100">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">RCMIS: Red Corner Management Information System</h1>
            <p class="text-gray-500 text-base mb-6">Engineering a multi-tiered hospitality platform mapping Office Automation (OAS), Management Information (MIS), and Executive Support (ESS) architectures.</p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs font-semibold">
                <span class="bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Systems Analysis & Design</span>
                <span class="bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Cross-Subsystem Database</span>
                <span class="bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Operational Dashboard</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 space-y-10">
        
        <section>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation text-red-500 mr-2"></i>The Operational Bottleneck</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Red-Corner Hotel and Residences operates an 18-room hotel along with 4 commercial leasing spaces[cite: 9]. Management faced massive friction due to operational fragmentation across its mixed-use business model[cite: 9, 10]:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
                <li><strong>Information Asymmetry & Double Bookings:</strong> Daily reservations from walk-ins and disparate third-party online platforms (Agoda, Airbnb, Facebook) were maintained on unsynchronized logs, leading to frequent double bookings and customer hostility[cite: 13, 16, 24].</li>
                <li><strong>Utility Billing Overhead:</strong> Monthly commercial and residential submeter tracking was recorded entirely in physical notebooks, requiring tedious manual calculations via basic spreadsheet templates across inconsistent tenant start dates[cite: 21, 57, 58].</li>
                <li><strong>Logistics and Staffing Friction:</strong> Room inventory, item restocking requests, and employee bi-weekly scheduling configurations were handled through offline communication channels, creating administrative blind spots[cite: 54, 56, 61].</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-diagram-project text-blue-500 mr-2"></i>Proposed Subsystem Integration</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                The RCMIS engineering model resolves these inefficiencies by linking walk-in and digital online booking protocols directly to a unified database cluster[cite: 139]. The system design introduces four primary data pipelines[cite: 76]:
            </p>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
                <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center"><i class="fa-solid fa-hotel text-blue-500 mr-1.5"></i> Dual-Database Booking Subsystem</h4>
                    Isolates real-time reservation schedules from active room statuses to prevent transactional lockups, immediately reflecting check-in/out updates across channels[cite: 78, 94].
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center"><i class="fa-solid fa-calculator text-emerald-500 mr-1.5"></i> Semi-Automated Tenant Billing</h4>
                    Consolidates water and electricity submeter data inputs to instantly compute weighted consumption totals, taxes, penalties, and lease dues[cite: 8, 70, 99].
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center"><i class="fa-solid fa-boxes-stacked text-amber-500 mr-1.5"></i> Real-Time Inventory Control</h4>
                    Monitors guest amenity usage and cleaning supplies, flagging automated reorder alerts when inventory drops below designated audit thresholds[cite: 34, 204, 205].
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
                    <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-days text-indigo-500 mr-1.5"></i> Collaborative Staff Scheduler</h4>
                    Generates balanced bi-weekly shift matrices by automatically matching institutional labor needs with individual employee shift preference profiles[cite: 72, 83].
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3"><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line text-indigo-500 mr-2"></i>Executive Support & Analytics Dashboard</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                To serve executive operations requirements, RCMIS abstracts relational data out of secondary subsystem databases into a high-level administrative intelligence layer[cite: 7, 79, 84]:
            </p>
            <div class="bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 p-5 rounded-xl border border-gray-800 space-y-3 text-sm font-mono">
                <p class="text-emerald-400 font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">// High-Fidelity Analytic Modeling Views</p>
                <p><span class="text-indigo-400">● Channels Analysis:</span> Visualizes comparative percentages of walk-in versus online revenue distributions[cite: 184].</p>
                <p><span class="text-indigo-400">● Occupancy Optimization:</span> Tracks dynamic daily utilization indicators to predict high-traffic calendar blocks[cite: 189].</p>
                <p><span class="text-indigo-400">● Financial Ledger Aggregation:</span> Pulls real-time transactional aggregates calculating current monthly revenues, daily income flows, and pending balances[cite: 133, 186, 188].</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
            <h3 class="text-gray-900 font-bold mb-3 flex items-center text-sm uppercase tracking-wide">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-lock text-indigo-600 mr-2"></i> Non-Functional System Compliance
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
                The technical proposal enforces localized data confidentiality standards[cite: 104, 118]. Sensitive financial payment tracking fields are designated for field-level encryption, while role-based permission boundaries restrict schedule manipulation and database updates solely to authorized administrative groups[cite: 85, 105, 117].
            </p>
        </section>

    </article>

